xByteIdentical` MUST NOT compare a version column and the file header MUST call out `updated_at` as the SOLE trigger-managed drift anchor (the BEFORE UPDATE set_updated_at trigger is the load-bearing anchor; a missing organization_id predicate would surface as updated_at drift even when every other column happened to look right). Mandatory test shape (the 8 tests this file lands, adapted from BE-0458): Insert(orgA)DoesNotTouchOrgB (byte-identity over queued + running-with-live-lease + idempotency-collide bystanders), Insert(orgA)DoesNotChangeOrgBRowCount, InsertSameIdempotencyKeyInTwoTenantsBothPersist (positive direction + per-tenant FindByIdempotencyKey round-trip), GetCrossTenantReturnsNotFoundAndDoesNotEcho (typed apierr.NotFound + substring no-leak on idempotency_key/request_id/correlation_id/project_id), FindByIdempotencyKeyCrossTenantDoesNotLeak (returns (zero, false, nil) + zero-value field-by-field no-leak), <StateMutation>CrossTenantLeavesOrgABystandersByteIdentical (the table's single mutating surface attempted by orgB on orgA's id -- Cancel for deployments, Transition(..., cancelled, mut) for jobs -- MUST surface as apierr.NotFound NOT Conflict, because the FOR UPDATE SELECT under (organization_id, id) returns ErrNoRows BEFORE the state-machine validator runs; bystanders include the named target + queued sibling + running sibling carrying a live lease), ListByOrganizationCrossTenantReturnsEmptyAndDoesNotLeakTotal (empty slice + side-effect-free read + per-tenant COUNT(*) invariance), OrganizationDeleteCascadeIsTenantScoped (orgA deletion cascades only to orgA's rows; orgB rows survive byte-identical -- include a row carrying a live lease to anchor lease_owner/lease_deadline/started_at). Always document in the file header what the file DELIBERATELY DELEGATES (composite-FK cross-tenant-parent path pinned by invariants story, closed-set / lifecycle CHECKs / state-machine matrix / lease bookkeeping / claimer pinned by subsystem story, redactor + payload marshalling pinned by internal_test) so a future reader does not mistake the omission for a coverage gap. When the table's worker-side claimer is INTENTIONALLY NOT tenant-scoped (e.g. ClaimNext SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED across all tenants), call it out explicitly in the header rationale. Forward-applicable to any future tenant-isolation story whose table follows the (subsystem-tests + invariants-tests + table-has-no-version-column) shape (e.g. future job_attempts / dokploy_refs if their repos land before their PRD stories).
ralph/progress.txt:44:- Repository tenant-isolation tests for an **APPEND-ONLY CHILD table whose ONLY public mutation surface is Append() inside a *Tx, anchored by a composite FK (organization_id, deployment_id) to a tenant-scoped parent table with ON DELETE CASCADE, whose row body has NO version column AND NO updated_at column AND NO Update/Delete surface (BEFORE UPDATE trigger rejects every UPDATE at the SQL level), AND whose tenant teardown is reachable only TRANSITIVELY via parent-deployment-cascade OR parent-organization-cascade** (BE-0460 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/deployment_event_tenant_isolation_test.go). Structurally distinct from BE-0458 (deployments — lifecycle-bearing table with version + updated_at trigger pair and a Cancel state-transition surface) in five load-bearing ways: (a) there is NO bump_version trigger AND NO set_updated_at trigger to anchor a cross-row UPDATE detection, because the BEFORE UPDATE trigger rejects every UPDATE outright; the bystander byte-identity assertion is therefore really proving Append's INSERT statement never even ATTEMPTS a write outside the supplied (organization_id, deployment_id) tuple. (b) The cross-tenant guard test must seed a SYMMETRIC PAIR of forged Append attempts — (orgA, bravoDep) AND (orgB, alphaDep) — and probe deployment_events by the forged ids to assert count = 0 for BOTH; a single direction would miss a regression that derived organization_id from the deployment row at write time, AND a missing forged-id-was-never-persisted probe would miss a buggy retry loop that swallowed the FK error after a phantom INSERT. (c) The cascade variants are TRANSITIVE and must be tested at BOTH depths separately — parent-deployment delete cascade (composite FK ON DELETE CASCADE on deployments(organization_id, id)) AND parent-organization delete cascade (the transitive chain organizations -> deployments -> deployment_events) — because each FK leg's organization_id scoping must be proven independently; a regression that dropped the organization_id leg of either FK would surface as either a bravo row vanishing or its byte content drifting. (d) The "soft-deleted rows where applicable" acceptance-criteria phrase narrows to "where applicable": deployment_events has no soft-delete column and no Delete repository surface, so cascade is the analogous proof and is the substitute test surface — the file header MUST document this delegation explicitly so a future reader does not mistake the absence for a coverage gap. (e) The metadata column is jsonb stored as []byte; bystander byte-identity uses bytes.Equal not json equivalence (a regression that stripped or reordered keys would defeat json equivalence but survive bytes.Equal — and the test wants to catch ANY rewrite, semantic or representational). The 8-test shape (Append-bystander-byte-identity across queued+running+progress peers / Append-row-count-invariant / Append-foreign-parent-deployment-rejected-BOTH-directions-with-forged-id-not-persisted+bystander-byte-identity / GetByID-cross-tenant-NotFound-with-no-leak (message/metadata key/value/request_id/correlation_id/event_type/deployment_id) / ListByDeployment-cross-tenant-empty-and-counts-unchanged across per-org AND per-deployment probes / ListByDeployment-foreign-deployment-id-of-SAME-tenant-returns-empty (composite (organization_id, deployment_id) probe distinct from "foreign org+foreign deployment") / parent-deployment-delete-cascade-is-tenant-scoped across queued+running+progress orgB peers / parent-organization-delete-cascade-is-tenant-scoped) leaves BE-0459's invariants surface (CRUD/append-only-trigger/closed-set-event_type/composite-FK/duplicate-id/nil-tx/rollback/metadata-redaction/caller-supplied-occurred_at/cascade-on-deployment) untouched. Helpers reused from BE-0459: rawDeploymentEventRow, loadDeploymentEventRowByID, countDeploymentEventRowsForDeployment, mintDeploymentEventID, runAppendDeploymentEventOrFail, seedDeploymentEvent; from BE-0458: seedTwoTenantDeploymentFixture, twoTenantDeploymentFixture type; from BE-0457: seedQueuedDeployment; from store_test: seedOrg/seedProject/seedEnvironment/seedService, newStore, containsValue. New helpers introduced (unique to this file): twoTenantDeploymentEventFixture + seedTwoTenantDeploymentEventFixture (the two-tenant boilerplate that ALSO seeds one parent deployment per tenant, because events need a parent deployment as the FK target — a pure two-tenant org/proj/env/svc fixture is insufficient for events), assertDeploymentEventByteIdentical (anchored on every column INCLUDING metadata []byte via bytes.Equal; NO version/updated_at columns to anchor cross-row UPDATE detection), countDeploymentEventRowsForOrg (per-tenant aggregate variant of countDeploymentEventRowsForDeployment — the cascade tests need both, per-tenant is the cascade-scoped probe, per-deployment is the Append-scoped probe). Forward-applicable to any tenant-isolation story whose table is an append-only child anchored by a composite FK to a tenant-scoped parent with cascade (e.g. future audit_events / job_events / log lines stories).
ralph/progress.txt:72:- Verification-suite single-file multi-surface static-test, lifecycle-projection-chokepoint instance (BE-0408 pattern, internal/release/verification_suite_deployment_lifecycle_e2e_static_test.go + internal/controlplane/store/deployment_lifecycle_e2e_canonical_test.go's new canonical pair TestDeploymentLifecycleE2ECoversCallSites + TestDeploymentLifecycleE2EPreservesContractUnderContention + SECURITY.md "## Deployment Lifecycle End-to-End Tests" section AND a new row in the Required Verification Gates table + internal/release/AGENTS.md "## Verification suite: deployment lifecycle end-to-end tests (BE-0408)" subsection; THIRTIETH worked instance of the BE-0379..BE-0407 verification-suite mega-pattern. Canonical command `go test -run TestDeploymentLifecycleE2E ./...`, CI step name `Deployment lifecycle end-to-end tests`, verify.sh prefix #32 inserted between BE-0407's #31 and the trailing optionals renumbered #32-#36 → #33-#37 in the same edit (with the BE-0400 external-smoke static-test constants `# 36 → # 37` and synthetic-fixture `# 35 → # 36` updated to match, plus BE-0400's trailing-optional commentary `#32-#35 → #33-#36`). Three forward-applicable extensions specific to the FIRST lifecycle-projection chokepoint (a slog.LogValuer pure projection on a closed-set lifecycle-state-machine row): (1) `slog TEXT AND JSON HANDLERS BOTH EMIT A time= ATTRIBUTE THAT BREAKS DETERMINISTIC ROUND-TRIP ASSERTIONS — INSTALL A ReplaceAttr HOOK THAT DROPS slog.TimeKey AT THE TOP-LEVEL GROUP ONLY (return slog.Attr{} when len(groups)==0 && a.Key==slog.TimeKey)`. Scope the drop to top-level groups so a customer-named attribute called `time` inside the projected group is still asserted on. Forward-applicable to every verification story whose chokepoint is a slog.LogValuer and whose canonical pair asserts repeat-call determinism on the rendered slog form. (2) `LIFECYCLE CHOKEPOINTS (closed-set rows whose terminal-vs-non-terminal enum classification implies a database CHECK on a sibling timestamp column) MUST PIN THE DATABASE-CHECK INVARIANT AT THE GO PROJECTION INSIDE THE CANONICAL PAIR's CLOSED-SET SELF-CHECK SEQUENCE`. The deployments_finished_consistent table CHECK becomes self-check #4 here: non-terminal status (queued, running) ⇒ nil FinishedAt; terminal status (succeeded, failed, cancelled, rolled_back) ⇒ set FinishedAt. Otherwise an in-memory regression that violates the CHECK only surfaces against a live Postgres; targeted canonical-pair gates do not. Forward-applicable to every verification story whose chokepoint is a row from a table whose closed-set status column has a sibling-column CHECK constraint. (3) `THE STRUCTURAL WHITELIST/BLACKLIST ASSERTION FOR A slog.LogValuer SHOULD DRIVE THROUGH THE JSON HANDLER (not the text handler) SO A REGRESSION THAT SWITCHED THE HANDLER STILL TRIPS THE CONTRACT`. The redaction contract isn't "this text never contains this string" (defeated by an escape change); it's "this group projects these keys and not these keys". JSON-route the projection, json.Unmarshal into map[string]any, assert keys whitelist + blacklist. The text-handler canary still fires for the secret-marker absence canary; both surfaces should be asserted side-by-side. Forward-applicable to every verification story whose chokepoint is a slog.LogValuer with a documented field whitelist. One canonical-pair-package gotcha worth pinning forward: `WHEN THE CHOKEPOINT'S EXPORTED API LIVES ON A VALUE RECEIVER OF A TYPE DECLARED IN THE PARENT PACKAGE (here store.Deployment with LogValue() on the value receiver), THE CANONICAL PAIR FILE GOES IN package <parent>_test AND IMPORTS THE PARENT PACKAGE — mirrors BE-0379..BE-0407 convention; no white-box `package store` test needed`. The chokepoint is `package store_test`'s view of `(store.Deployment).LogValue()`, with helper renders (`deploymentLifecycleRenderLogValue`, `deploymentLifecycleStructuredLogValue`) wrapping the slog API. Load-bearing invariant unchanged: ONE FILE, SIX SURFACES, SELF-CHECK; drift on any surface fails ONE test, not six.
