ralph/progress.txt:19569:  - internal/controlplane/policy/job_retry_policy_test.go (new, 8 tests + 28 subtests): canonical fixture ids canonicalJobRetryProjectID / canonicalJobRetrySiblingID (distinct from canonicalJobReadProjectID and canonicalJobReadByIDProjectID so the three job matrices cannot accidentally share state through a future shared helper). Four resource-builder helpers — jobRetryOrgResource (org-rooted), jobRetryProjectResource (project-owned), jobRetryEnvResource (env-owned), jobRetryServiceResource (service-owned) — model every owning-scope shape the bare-id retry resolver will construct when it looks up the row's owner before deciding. The {job_id} segment is treated as a routing artefact, not a policy boundary; the load-bearing pin is that a service-scoped key cannot escalate to a parent- or sibling-owned job row by id, and a staging-env-scoped key cannot retry a production-owned job row by id.
ralph/progress.txt:19570:  - Tests cover: TestJobRetryPolicyMatrixRoles (CapDeploy four-role allow Owner/Admin/Developer/CI ReasonAllowedByRole; Viewer/Support deny ReasonDeniedNoCapability), TestJobRetryPolicyRevokedAndExpiredKeys (disabled-principal short-circuit ReasonDeniedPrincipalDisabled even with Owner underlying role), TestJobRetryPolicyWrongOrganizationPrincipal (ALL six built-in roles including Support denied ReasonDeniedCrossTenant — CapDeploy is OUTSIDE the engine's CapRead+CapSupport cross-tenant exception, the load-bearing distinction from job.read's cross-tenant matrix), TestJobRetryPolicyProjectGrantContainment (admin-on-target allows; admin-on-target denies org-root and sibling-project; ci-on-target allows; viewer-on-target denies no-capability — pins both scope-containment and CapDeploy at the project-grant path), TestJobRetryPolicyEnvironmentGrantContainment (staging-Admin grant denies org-root and parent-project owned, allows staging-env-owned, denies production-env-owned, denies production env.write — pins the staging-never-widens-to-production rule for the mutating verb), TestJobRetryPolicyServiceGrantContainment (svcA-Admin grant denies org-root, parent-project, parent-env owned job rows; denies parent env.write and sibling service.update; denies sibling svc_b-owned job row; allows own svc_a-owned job row — full containment matrix at the deepest grant scope), TestJobRetryPolicyOrgGrantCapabilityMatrix (CI/Developer allow ReasonAllowedByGrant; Viewer/Support deny ReasonDeniedNoCapability via the org-grant path — pins the CapDeploy split with scope held constant), TestJobRetryPolicyForeignHomeOrgGrant (stolen-scoped-key guard: grant for orgA carried by orgB principal against orgB resource → ReasonDeniedNoCapability via the engine's `g.Scope.OrganizationID != principal.OrganizationID` filter).
