ralph/progress.txt:35024:- What was implemented: Added public contract tests for `POST /v1/jobs/{job_id}/retry`, covering stdout/stderr silence, success/authn/authz request-log redaction, dependency-cause redaction, request_id propagation on error envelopes, and authenticated OpenAPI metadata including `{job_id}` and `x-required-action`.
ralph/progress.txt:35025:- Files changed: `internal/controlplane/httpapi/jobs_retry_contract_test.go`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
ralph/progress.txt:35026:- Verification run: `gofmt -w .`; `go mod tidy`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/httpapi -run 'TestRetryJob|TestGetJob'`; `go test ./...`; `go test -race ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test -race ./internal/controlplane/...`; `golangci-lint run ./...`; commit hook `scripts/verify.sh --strict --release` including full tests, race tests, focused backend suites, `govulncheck`, `staticcheck`, `golangci-lint`, `goreleaser check`, and snapshot release build.
ralph/progress.txt:35030:  - Retry job contract tests can reuse the existing `fakeJobReader` because it satisfies both the resolver `GetJob` path and the mutation `RetryJob` path used by `NewHandler`.
