- Verification run: `gofmt -w .`; `go mod tidy`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/httpapi -run 'TestRetryJob|TestGetJob'`; `go test ./...`; `go test -race ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test -race ./internal/controlplane/...`; `golangci-lint run ./...`; commit hook `scripts/verify.sh --strict --release` including full tests, race tests, focused backend suites, `govulncheck`, `staticcheck`, `golangci-lint`, `goreleaser check`, and snapshot release build.
- Results: All listed checks passed. Direct `goimports` was not installed in this environment, so it was not run outside the hook.
- Remaining risks or follow-ups: Live Dokploy smoke was not run; the strict hook reported it is opt-in and requires `YALLA_EXTERNAL_DOKPLOY=1` with live Dokploy configuration.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Retry job contract tests can reuse the existing `fakeJobReader` because it satisfies both the resolver `GetJob` path and the mutation `RetryJob` path used by `NewHandler`.
  - For bare-job mutating endpoints, dependency-cause redaction should be tested with an org-wide deploy-capable principal so resolver fallback to org scope still permits the handler to surface the typed dependency error.
